BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:finland-fi-pay-transparency@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Finland: Pay transparency bill: pay-gap reporting via the Incomes R
 egister (draft)
DESCRIPTION:Proposed from 1 Jan 2027. On 9 July 2026 the government propose
 d amendments to equal-pay legislation implementing the EU pay transparency
  directive\, with entry into force proposed for 1 January 2027. Employers 
 regularly employing at least 100 workers would report gender pay-gap data 
 through the Incomes Register.\n\nSource: https://valtioneuvosto.fi/-/12711
 39/hallitus-esittaa-lakimuutoksia-palkkauksen-lapinakyvyyden-vahvistamisek
 si\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/finland.html#fi-p
 ay-transparency\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Sources
  last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/finland.html#fi-pay-transpa
 rency
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-uk-upcoming@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Unfair dismissal qualifying period cut to six month
 s
DESCRIPTION:Starts in January 2027\; the source does not state the day. Eff
 ective January 2027. Under the Employment Rights Act timetable\, the unfai
 r dismissal qualifying period is reduced to six months\, and the cap on th
 e compensatory award is removed\, from January 2027. The reduced qualifyin
 g period applies to dismissals taking place from that date.\n\nSource: htt
 ps://www.davidsonmorris.com/employment-rights-act-timeline/\nDetails: http
 s://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/united-kingdom.html#uk-upcoming\n\
 nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Sources last checked 1 Oc
 tober 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/united-kingdom.html#uk-upco
 ming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-uk-reporting-upcoming@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270406
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270407
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Mandatory payrolling of benefits in kind\, phased f
 rom April 2027
DESCRIPTION:Phase 1: 6 Apr 2027. Payrolling of benefits in kind becomes man
 datory in phases. From 6 April 2027 the most common benefits - company car
 s\, car and van fuel\, vans and medical benefit - must be reported and tax
 ed in real time through RTI payroll software. From 6 April 2028 most remai
 ning benefits in kind are mandated\, except employer-provided loans and ac
 commodation.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/changes
 -to-reporting-of-benefits-in-kind-from-april-2027/mandatory-reporting-of-b
 enefits-in-kind-in-real-time-information-rti-from-april-2027\nDetails: htt
 ps://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/united-kingdom.html#uk-reporting-
 upcoming\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Sources last c
 hecked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/united-kingdom.html#uk-repo
 rting-upcoming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:belgium-be-reporting-upcoming@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Belgium: "Loon-datatransfer" tool to replace DmfA
DESCRIPTION:Voluntary from 2027. As part of RSZ's e-gov modernisation\, a n
 ew "loon-datatransfer" (wage data transfer) tool will be available for vol
 untary use and testing from 1 January 2027\, become mandatory from 1 Janua
 ry 2028\, and the DmfA submission itself will be abolished from 1 January 
 2030. RSZ began sending informational letters to employers about the trans
 ition from 28 May 2026.\n\nSource: https://www.unizo.be/berichten/nieuws/i
 nformatiebrieven-rsz\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries
 /belgium.html#be-reporting-upcoming\n\nFor information only\, not legal or
  tax advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/belgium.html#be-reporting-u
 pcoming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:czechia-cz-reporting-upcoming@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Czech Republic: EU Pay Transparency Directive - phased Labour Code 
 amendment (draft)
DESCRIPTION:Mostly from 1 Jan 2027. The draft amendment to the Labour Code\
 , published on 27 March 2026\, transposing the directive foresees phased e
 ntry into force: most provisions are expected to take effect from 1 Januar
 y 2027\, while regular pay-gap reporting\, the related pay assessment and 
 corrective measures\, and employees' right to request written pay informat
 ion are expected from 1 January 2028.\n\nSource: https://www.ey.com/cs_cz/
 technical/tax/tax-alerts/2026/03/transparentnost-odmenovani-1-cast-novela-
 zakoniku-prace-zverejnena\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/coun
 tries/czech-republic.html#cz-reporting-upcoming\n\nFor information only\, 
 not legal or tax advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/czech-republic.html#cz-repo
 rting-upcoming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:estonia-ee-reporting-upcoming@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270402
SUMMARY:Estonia: Data-based TSD replaces the tax declaration form
DESCRIPTION:Effective 1 Apr 2027. The Tax and Customs Board (MTA) is moving
  to data-based reporting: the accountant will send transaction data to the
  tax authority\, which calculates the taxes itself. MTA confirmed the new 
 system takes effect on 1 April 2027.\n\nSource: https://www.raamatupidaja.
 ee/uudised/2025/01/20/mta-plaanib-raamatupidamiskirjendite-pohise-tsd-kasu
 tuselevottu-2026-aasta-lopus\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/c
 ountries/estonia.html#ee-reporting-upcoming\n\nFor information only\, not 
 legal or tax advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/estonia.html#ee-reporting-u
 pcoming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eg-eg-insurable-wage-2027@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Egypt: Insurable wage limits rise again in 2027
DESCRIPTION:Effective 1 January 2027. Under the scheduled annual increases\
 , the minimum insurable wage becomes EGP 3\,200 and the maximum EGP 19\,30
 0 per month in 2027.\n\nSource: https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/egypt/individ
 ual/other-taxes\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/egyp
 t.html#eg-insurable-wage-2027\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax a
 dvice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/egypt.html#eg-insurable-wag
 e-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
